    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0801" n="697" xml:id="pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5052: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting Secretary
                            of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-18T12:00:00+08:00">April 18,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 18—5:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My April 13, 8 p.m., and April 18, 11 a.m.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d744-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Lampson and I have just been
                        informed that Quo is returning from
                        Nanking tomorrow expecting to resume negotiations with the Japanese.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>With reference to my telegram of April 13, 8 p.m., Lampson has information from his Secretary
                        of State for Foreign Affairs to the effect that Committee of Nineteen at
                        Geneva will adopt second alternative mentioned in paragraph 5 thereof and
                        will probably pass a resolution following lines suggested in paragraph 6
                        thereof.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>I propose to return to Shanghai on April 20th as Lampson and I consider that the time is
                        probably ripe for bringing local negotiations to a conclusion.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d744-f1" n="67" xml:id="d744-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed; in it the Minister reported, “I am going tomorrow morning by
                    plane to Nanking…” (393.1111 Baker,
                        Charles/70).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
